SDL2: no default KMSDRM arrow cursor unless SDL_KMSDRM_DEFAULT_CURSOR=1

SPDX-License-Identifier: Zlib
Local alteration (v1.1.1 T3): the R35S has no pointing device, yet SDL's
KMSDRM backend put its default arrow on the VOP cursor plane (64x64 at
0,0) in every SDL app that does not hide it itself (PortMaster's GUI,
Godot frt and doukutsu-rs ports). Upstream muOS hides it with a preloaded
SDL_ShowCursor(0) shim (libmucursor.so), which cannot reach SDL loaded
through ctypes (PortMaster's pysdl2) and is undone by apps that show the
cursor again. Without a default cursor SDL shows nothing until an app sets
its own (SDL_CreateCursor / SDL_SetCursor still work).

--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmmouse.c
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmmouse.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 
 #ifdef SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_KMSDRM
 
+#include "SDL_hints.h"
 #include "SDL_kmsdrmvideo.h"
 #include "SDL_kmsdrmmouse.h"
 #include "SDL_kmsdrmdyn.h"
@@ -412,7 +413,8 @@
     /* Only create the default cursor for this display if we haven't done so before,
        we don't want several cursors to be created for the same display. */
     if (!dispdata->default_cursor_init) {
-        SDL_SetDefaultCursor(KMSDRM_CreateDefaultCursor());
+        if (SDL_GetHintBoolean("SDL_KMSDRM_DEFAULT_CURSOR", SDL_FALSE))
+            SDL_SetDefaultCursor(KMSDRM_CreateDefaultCursor());
         dispdata->default_cursor_init = SDL_TRUE;
     }
 }
